comment.narrative:
1.	Zero direct project beneficiaries disaggregated by gender (individual people);
2.	Zero ha Terrestrial protected areas under improved management for conservation and sustainable use;
3.	Zero ha Area of restored wetlands; 
4.	Zero metric tons of CO2 eq Greenhouse Gas Emissions Mitigated;
5.	There are no any approved new/amended regulations/policies/laws directly related to improving status, management and financing regimes of wetlands;
6.	There are no any approved new/amended regulations/policies/laws related to prioritization of the financing of wetlands  through the  National Ecological Fund;
7.	 METT score for the targeted national Pas: Lower Prut Biosphere Reserve 31 and Royal Forest Nature Reserve 57;
8.	Stable status/positive changes in the population of globally significant biodiversity at the targeted Pas- Baseline: as indicated in the METT scorecards;
9.	Hectares of lakes and riparian ecosystems restored in the Lower Prut Biosphere Reserve - Baseline to be established at project inception;
10.	Zero hectares of floodplain areas restored in and around the Royal Forest Nature Reserve;
11.	Percentage of increase in monetary income to targeted entrepreneurs derived from sustainable wetland use and facilitated tourism (gender disaggregated) - Baseline to be established at project inception;
12.	1300 visitors in Lower Prut Biosphere reserve for the 2020 year;
13.	There are no any knowledge products related to wetlands conservation considerations mainstreaming into policies, laws and regulations, developed and disseminated. Project knowledge products include, where feasible, an analysis of gender equity/empowerment in relation with the specific knowledge topic.
14.	Limited access to the best available knowledge and practice, through project-supported knowledge products and training
15.	There are no an available Monitoring and Evaluation reports Evaluative knowledge to project partners
